7
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:35,360
Before we go any further, it's probably helpful to define fascism, which is something that nobody in these conversations ever seems to do, which is why they get so emotionally heated.

8
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:39,780
Fascism is a form of palingenetic ultranationalism.

9
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:45,100
Now that word palingenetic comes from palingenesis, the idea of a national rebirth.

10
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:55,440
Fascism is obsessed with a cult of national purity and an idea of a mythic golden past that must be returned to through a form of national rebirth.

11
00:00:55,440 --> 00:01:15,240
The nation, which is imagined to be humiliated and threatened on the international stage, must be reborn through a broad-based revolutionary nationalist movement that defines itself against the backdrop of political gridlock and rejects both liberal reformism and leftist class struggle.

12
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:17,200
Are you tracking with me so far?

13
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:21,940
Fascism is a style of politics, not a form of government.

14
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:25,940
It is a process, not an end result.

15
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:39,740
While fascism tends to end with jackbooted thugs in the night and boxcars to Dachau or slit trenches in Treblinka, it usually starts as a protest movement inside a broader conservative coalition.

16
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:45,780
A conservative commenter recently replied to one of my posts and said, and I think a way that was tongue in cheek.

17
